{"parentUuid":"c5837ba8-89fa-4129-9ab6-68d579959139","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"de187d87-78e0-4fae-b609-5bd6538472df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ftGwJ6FRr1GoNeYGzE2ee","type":"tool_result","content":"Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:350:        patch.persist_as = arguments[\"persistAs\"].get<std::string>();\nAgent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:929:                 \"Saving a preset is the person's: your settings_preview_patch with persistAs shows them a card with Save \"\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:140:           (arguments[\"scope\"] != \"object\" && arguments[\"persistAs\"].is_string() &&\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:141:            !arguments[\"persistAs\"].get_ref<const std::string&>().empty() && optional_text(arguments, \"persistAs\"));\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:166:        if (!(apply ? has_only(arguments, {\"scope\", \"target\", \"changes\", \"persistAs\", \"expectedSessionId\", \"expectedRevision\"}) :\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:167:                      has_only(arguments, {\"scope\", \"target\", \"changes\", \"persistAs\"})) ||\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:987:                        \"issue suggests unless the user gave one. Without persistAs a change stays unsaved, which only the \"\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1090:         \"Validate an atomic settings patch, and persistAs, without changing anything; use the returned sessionId and revision when applying. A setting that holds one value per extruder or nozzle takes the same number of values, separated by commas. object checks the patch as overrides on that object: settings that apply to the whole print (skirt, travel speed, spiral vase and the like) are refused with unsupported_scope, and no dependencies are predicted because OrcaSlicer keeps object overrides as written. A filament or printer preset that is not the one being edited changes only by being saved (not_selected without persistAs). A warning with code skipped_confirmation is a confirmation OrcaSlicer asks of a person who makes that change, or saves it, by hand, in its own words. The patch skips it and applies as sent, so it is yours to settle before applying: go ahead; go ahead and tell the user; or, when the answer is the user's to give (it depends on what the object is for, or it accepts a risk to their printer), ask them first. Its suggestions are the values OrcaSlicer's Yes would set; add them to the patch to accept them.\",\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1091:         object_schema({{\"scope\", settings_scope}, {\"target\", settings_target}, {\"changes\", changes_input}, {\"persistAs\", persist_as}},\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1096:         \"Apply an atomic settings patch immediately. Requires the sessionId and revision from a preview of the same scope, target, changes and persistAs; edits to the model since that preview do not matter, a settings change does. A process, filament or printer change is not undone by project Undo; an object override is. With persistAs the preset is saved as well, and savedAs names what it was saved as.\",","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e4d9c229-6751-48ef-8705-bff8057730f5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:29:00.888Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Agent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:350:        patch.persist_as = arguments[\"persistAs\"].get<std::string>();\nAgent/ToolExecutionCoordinator.cpp:929:                 \"Saving a preset is the person's: your settings_preview_patch with persistAs shows them a card with Save \"\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:140:           (arguments[\"scope\"] != \"object\" && arguments[\"persistAs\"].is_string() &&\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:141:            !arguments[\"persistAs\"].get_ref<const std::string&>().empty() && optional_text(arguments, \"persistAs\"));\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:166:        if (!(apply ? has_only(arguments, {\"scope\", \"target\", \"changes\", \"persistAs\", \"expectedSessionId\", \"expectedRevision\"}) :\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:167:                      has_only(arguments, {\"scope\", \"target\", \"changes\", \"persistAs\"})) ||\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:987:                        \"issue suggests unless the user gave one. Without persistAs a change stays unsaved, which only the \"\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1090:         \"Validate an atomic settings patch, and persistAs, without changing anything; use the returned sessionId and revision when applying. A setting that holds one value per extruder or nozzle takes the same number of values, separated by commas. object checks the patch as overrides on that object: settings that apply to the whole print (skirt, travel speed, spiral vase and the like) are refused with unsupported_scope, and no dependencies are predicted because OrcaSlicer keeps object overrides as written. A filament or printer preset that is not the one being edited changes only by being saved (not_selected without persistAs). A warning with code skipped_confirmation is a confirmation OrcaSlicer asks of a person who makes that change, or saves it, by hand, in its own words. The patch skips it and applies as sent, so it is yours to settle before applying: go ahead; go ahead and tell the user; or, when the answer is the user's to give (it depends on what the object is for, or it accepts a risk to their printer), ask them first. Its suggestions are the values OrcaSlicer's Yes would set; add them to the patch to accept them.\",\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1091:         object_schema({{\"scope\", settings_scope}, {\"target\", settings_target}, {\"changes\", changes_input}, {\"persistAs\", persist_as}},\nAgent/ToolRegistry.cpp:1096:         \"Apply an atomic settings patch immediately. Requires the sessionId and revision from a preview of the same scope, target, changes and persistAs; edits to the model since that preview do not matter, a settings change does. A process, filament or printer change is not undone by project Undo; an object override is. With persistAs the preset is saved as well, and savedAs names what it was saved as.\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":f